{
  "_note": "Story 070 (owner request): chunky, satisfying button sounds, all made live with the Web Audio synth (oscillators and filtered noise): the game's own, never samples or imitations of any game. A button's kind: a disabled button is always 'blocked'; then data-sfx; then these selector lists in order (toggle, close, open, primary, secondary), else 'press'. Each voice is layers of tones (wave + MIDI notes played one after another, `step` apart; `bend` = semitones the pitch slides over the duration) or noise (`filterHz` = band-pass sweep from, to). `gain` levels sit under the SFX volume and master gain. minGapMs: no two button sounds closer than this. jitter: secondary taps vary in pitch by up to this share. duckGain: UI sounds while the client speaks. hapticMs: the haptic tick on a primary press (Comfort's vibration setting). tickEveryMs: the results count-up tick spacing. moveTolerancePx: a touch that moves more than this is a scroll (no sound).",
  "minGapMs": 40,
  "jitter": 0.05,
  "duckGain": 0.5,
  "hapticMs": 25,
  "tickEveryMs": 90,
